================================================================================
2. THE CATALOGUE DATA — CC BY-SA 4.0, and upstream terms
================================================================================

Applies to app/src/main/assets/catalogue/ and to tools/catalogue/data/.

These files are assembled from public sources and are NOT covered by the MIT
license above. The habitat and description prose is reused from Wikipedia under
CC BY-SA 4.0, which is a share-alike license: a derivative of that text has to
carry the same license. So the catalogue as a whole is offered under

    CC BY-SA 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

with these upstream terms underneath it, per field:

  Wikipedia prose (habitat, description)   CC BY-SA 4.0
  Wikimedia Commons reference images       per image; the credit and license
                                           travel with each entry in the JSON
  GBIF backbone taxonomy (names, class)    CC BY 4.0
  Dr. Duke's ethnobotanical database       CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication);
    (app/src/main/assets/catalogue/        the full dedication is in
     duke_ethnobot.json)                   catalogue/LICENSE-duke.txt

Reference images are referenced by URL rather than redistributed, and each
entry carries the author and license string Commons reports for it. The app
shows all of this at Settings -> Licenses and attribution, which renders
app/src/main/assets/licenses.md.

The edible tags and the short note naming a plant part and a season are this
project's own curation and fall under part 1, not under any upstream source.


